From: ManicardiMatteo87 <manicardi.matteo87@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:40:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] fix(motion): FAST top stride 74 mm, two ticks under the
 STOP proof at the swing peak (F3)

The fixture FAULT of 16/11 (suite F3, FAST preset 2, WALK_IK_OR_WORKSPACE with
refused_by STOP_PLAN at walk cycle 2.408) is the STOP proof's secant limit:
with a = 0 StopPlan accepts at most 2.405 rad/s at the walk drive (0.35 rad
residual, braking 84, 20 ms grid), 31.36 RAW ticks per release. At 80 mm the
front UPPER swing peak reads 31 ticks; 32 refuses the correction step and its
retry. Offline rig (production Motion, E -> F3, fixture and ground): every
refusal at cycle 2.408/4.408, RF_UPPER, 32 ticks.

No swing profile keeps 80 mm two ticks under: shifting the trapezoid moves the
peak from the front UPPER (late swing) to the hind LOWER (early swing), 30-31
ticks for every (ramp, ramp end) scanned. The peak scales with the speed, so
the FAST top stride goes from 80 to 74 mm (29.6 mm/s, the frontal joystick top
too): 29 ticks in every scenario (rig full scan, 0 refusals, box margin kept).
Presets 0-1, the swing profile, duty, height, lift, sway, drive, STOP/StopPlan
and every limit are unchanged; SLOW and STANDARD bit for bit.

- run_stop_secant_gate.sh: new offline gate, every sent reference of every
  mode, preset, joystick direction and transition and the suite's E -> F3
  sequence (flat, fixture tilt, slope, lag, late releases), secant + 1 tick
  inside the StopPlan frontier of its drive. a86c680: FAIL (FAST 31 ticks);
  this commit: PASS (FAST 29, margin 1.36 ticks; STANDARD preset 2 30, 0.36).
- Dashboard: FAST default label 30 mm/s (what modeLabels shows for 74/2.5),
  notes 29,6 mm/s; DOM test expectation follows.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
